# cache: bounded caching with pluggable eviction, in boru.
#
# STATUS — DESIGNED, NOT IMPLEMENTED.
#
# This module is a scaffold. The `Cache` namespace exported at the bottom
# is deliberately EMPTY. The argued design — what this library is (an
# EFFECT MEMOIZER, not a general-purpose cache), the measurement that
# decides that, the eviction policy roster, and the boru constraints that
# force each shape — lives in DESIGN.md at the repository root. Read it
# before adding anything here.
#
# The headline finding, because it governs every later choice: a map read
# costs ~63us on this runtime and a write ~3us, both O(1). A cache is only
# worth installing over work that costs substantially more than a lookup,
# so this library targets expensive EFFECTS (network, file, heavy parse)
# and explicitly not cheap pure computation, where it would be a net loss.
#
# --- representation ---
#
# Not yet fixed. DESIGN.md sections 5 and 9 record the candidate shape: a
# `flex` entry map plus an append-only `flex` ring and an integer hand
# (what CLOCK and SIEVE want), rather than the doubly-linked list a
# textbook LRU needs and boru cannot express well.
#
# Calling convention: forward args, receiver (the cache) LAST —
# `Cache.verb ...args c`, with the piping form `c Cache.verb ...args end`
# equally valid. Fixed now so the design cannot drift from it.
#
# Imported via `import "./cache.aql"`.

export "Cache" {
}
